{
  "id": "ss.relic.oldblood",
  "name": "Old blood",
  "description": "A puddle of blood that dried a long time ago: a flat irregular pool, the crust wine-dark with a lighter rim of the same red where it thinned at the edge, three rust-brown patches where the crust has lifted and gone matte, and one crack across it with its lower lip caught by the light. One small fresh drop sits on the upper-right edge, the only bright wet thing on the plate. The relic stops the ruins handing out Rares — the good blood has already been spilt and set — so the pool is old and the drop is what is left. The centre is kept the same value as the rim and broken up with the flakes so that a dark pool with a lighter edge does not read as a hole in the panel.",
